      "content": "1. WHAT IS A NOUN?"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Understanding Noun identification and its various types forms the fundamental basis of English grammar for SSC exams.",
        "Crucial distinction lies in Countable vs Uncountable Nouns, including common SSC traps with specific uncountable noun lists.",
        "Plural variations require special attention: irregular plurals, foreign plurals, nouns that look plural but are singular, and nouns existing only in plural.",
        "Agreement rules such as 'One Of', 'A Number Of' vs 'The Number Of', and Collective Noun logic are heavily tested high-probability topics.",
        "Possessive noun application involves distinct rules for joint versus separate possession."
      ],
      "id": "ikjyi5j"
